    <string name="whats_up_help">Shows deep-sky objects (nebulae, galaxies, clusters) that are currently above the horizon at your location.\n\n• Objects are sorted by altitude — higher = better positioned\n• Green icon: well-placed (above 30°), ideal for imaging\n• Grey icon: low in the sky (10–30°), possible but less ideal\n• Best results when used during astronomical darkness\n\nThis catalog includes ~27 popular astrophotography targets.</string>
